      "writtenOn": "2022-10-26T14:11:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently, this change will work. Thing may break if Go and Big Android modules are different. There is a plan for long term fix?",
      "revId": "d47355be06f4bd0cd0d894376a5202daeaf125af",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "20141a9d_f18324bb",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060959
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-26T16:53:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think there is anything to verify they\u0027re identical, so it seems quite risky : if a partner were to update the Go \u0026 non-go train separately in the same, what would happen?\n\nwe also don\u0027t have go-specific SDKs",
      "parentUuid": "9bfc5622_12f6a482",
      "revId": "d47355be06f4bd0cd0d894376a5202daeaf125af",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "690c854d_71bd1228",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944716
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-26T17:44:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This do require Go and non-go train not to be updated separately. For example, there is a Gantry work planned in Q1 2023 to provide a single partner zip with artifacts consisting of common module sdk and Go + non-Go prebuilt modules., which means that Go and non-Go would be from the same release branch.",
      "parentUuid": "20141a9d_f18324bb",
      "revId": "d47355be06f4bd0cd0d894376a5202daeaf125af",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "99b1ae50_157f1fc4",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1451833
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-26T21:45:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Zhi and Anton, I think we have agreed that the Module SDKs for Go and nonGo will be the same. With that assumption, I think this patch works for now? I do agree though that we need a long term fix and maybe re-think the way we do this check. I feel this check is being run too early as fundamentally only one apex ends up on a device, so why should the apex name from different rules be compared as an early check?",
      "parentUuid": "690c854d_71bd1228",
      "revId": "d47355be06f4bd0cd0d894376a5202daeaf125af",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a2a3c82_2a8f5afe",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1890055
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-27T12:53:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Most (Go, Big-Android) module pairs are built from the exact same code base and have the same version, and can reasonably be expected to have identical APIs (since we don\u0027t support different build flags for Go and Big-Android).\nHowever this is not the case for adservices, because the version of adservices for Big Android contains some functionality, was built from recent code, and has a higher version than the Go version, which is just the same empty stub we included in T-FRC. Therefore it\u0027s unlikely that the Go and Big-Android versions of adservices for November can both be compatible with a single module SDK.",
      "parentUuid": "99b1ae50_157f1fc4",
      "revId": "d47355be06f4bd0cd0d894376a5202daeaf125af",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3c020850_570b6241",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-27T13:20:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just to be clear, dexpreopting is an implementation dependency, so the dex jars in the two APEXes have to be built from the same sources with the same options, same proguarding, same toolchain, etc. Identical APIs isn\u0027t enough.",
      "parentUuid": "4a2a3c82_2a8f5afe",
      "revId": "d47355be06f4bd0cd0d894376a5202daeaf125af",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
